{"tool_name":"dyebias","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bioconductor-dyebias","version":"1.70.0","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/html/dyebias.html","license":"GPL-3","summary":"The GASSCO method for correcting for slide-dependent gene-specific dye bias","identifiers":["biotools:dyebias"],"description":"Many two-colour hybridizations suffer from a dye bias that is both gene-specific and slide-specific. The former depends on the content of the nucleotide used for labeling; the latter depends on the labeling percentage. The slide-dependency was hitherto not recognized, and made addressing the artefact impossible.  Given a reasonable number of dye-swapped pairs of hybridizations, or of same vs. same hybridizations, both the gene- and slide-biases can be estimated and corrected using the GASSCO method (Margaritis et al., Mol. Sys. Biol. 5:266 (2009), doi:10.1038/msb.2009.21)","license_file":"/lib/R/share/licenses/GPL-3","build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0,"rpaths":["lib/R/lib/","lib/"],"run_exports":""},"requirements":{"host":["bioconductor-biobase >=2.70.0,<2.71.0","bioconductor-marray >=1.88.0,<1.89.0","r-base"],"run":["bioconductor-biobase >=2.70.0,<2.71.0","bioconductor-marray >=1.88.0,<1.89.0","r-base"]},"source_url":["https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/dyebias_1.70.0.tar.gz","https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.22/bioc/src/contrib/Archive/dyebias/dyebias_1.70.0.tar.gz","https://bioarchive.galaxyproject.org/dyebias_1.70.0.tar.gz","https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/bioconductor-dyebias/bioconductor-dyebias_1.70.0_src_all.tar.gz"],"test":{"commands":["$R -e \"library('dyebias')\""]},"parent_recipe":{"name":"bioconductor-dyebias","path":"recipes/bioconductor-dyebias","version":"1.40.0"}},"biotools":{"id":"dyebias","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/dyebias","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Many two-colour hybridizations suffer from a dye bias that is both gene-specific and slide-specific. The former depends on the content of the nucleotide used for labeling; the latter depends on the labeling percentage. The slide-dependency was hitherto not recognized, and made addressing the artefact impossible.  Given a reasonable number of dye-swapped pairs of hybridizations, or of same vs. same hybridizations, both the gene- and slide-biases can be estimated and corrected using the GASSCO method (Margaritis et al., Mol. Sys. Biol. 5:266 (2009), doi:10.1038/msb.2009.21)","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:05:08Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-29T14:00:55Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.72.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:dyebias","credit":[{"name":"Philip Lijnzaad and Thanasis Margaritis"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/dyebias"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"}]}],"name":"dyebias","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/msb.2009.21"}],"topic":[{"term":"Microarray experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3518"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"dyebias","home":"https://bio.tools/dyebias","license":"GPL-3.0-only","version":"1.72.0","summary":"Many two-colour hybridizations suffer from a dye bias that is both gene-specific and slide-specific. The former depends on the content of the nucleotide used for labeling; the latter depends on the labeling percentage. The slide-dependency was hitherto not recognized, and made addressing the artefact impossible.  Given a reasonable number of dye-swapped pairs of hybridizations, or of same vs. same hybridizations, both the gene- and slide-biases can be estimated and corrected using the GASSCO method (Margaritis et al., Mol. Sys. Biol. 5:266 (2009), doi:10.1038/msb.2009.21)","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApp